+# Feature Specification: Rental Module
+
+**Created**: 2026-11-17 | **Status**: Draft
+
+**Input**: In-memory rental module for the booking desk: add equipment, quote, book. Cancellation is out of scope (policy recorded for later).
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing
+
+### User Story 1 - Quote a rental (P1)
+Desk staff ask what renting an item for a period costs.
+**Acceptance**:
+1. Given a board at 2500 cents/day, when quoting 2026-05-01T00:00:00Z to 2026-05-04T00:00:00Z, then total is 7500.
+2. Given an unknown item, or a period that is not whole UTC days / is empty / ends before it starts, then quoting fails with an error.
+
+### User Story 2 - Book a rental (P1)
+**Acceptance**:
+1. Given a free item, booking returns an id, item, period and total equal to the quote.
+2. Given an existing booking, booking the same item for an overlapping period fails; back-to-back periods (end == other's start) and other items are fine.
+3. A failed booking leaves no trace.
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: `createRentalService()` exported from `src/index.ts`, state in memory, independent per call.
+- **FR-002**: `addEquipment({id, kind, dailyPrice})`; kind is `board` or `sail`; dailyPrice a non-negative integer of euro cents; id unique non-empty string. Invalid input or duplicate id is rejected.
+- **FR-003**: `quote` returns `{itemId,start,end,total}`; total = days × dailyPrice (integer cents).
+- **FR-004**: `book` returns `{id,itemId,start,end,total}` with a unique booking id.
+- **FR-005**: Times are UTC ISO-8601 strings; periods start and end at 00:00:00 UTC, end is the start of the day after the last day, end strictly after start. Returned start/end are the canonical `YYYY-MM-DDT00:00:00.000Z` form.
+- **FR-006**: Same item cannot be booked for overlapping periods (half-open intervals).
+- **FR-007**: `quote`/`book` throw for unknown item or disallowed period; `book` also throws when not free.
+
+## Assumptions
+- Cancellation not implemented. Policy for later: cancelled < 24h before start → no refund, otherwise full refund (integer cents).
+- Booking does not check that the quote is in the future.
+- Quote does not check availability.
+
+## Success Criteria
+- All acceptance scenarios pass as automated tests.
